@H H_1160 := "does the from-scratch inference+learning MITOSIS engine need a metronome TICK to gate its cell-division growth, or is the tick EVENT/DERIVATIVE-driven? (the user's 틱이 있어야 되나?)" :: discovery [d=2026-06-12 status=🔴-CLOSED-NEGATIVE domain=MITOSIS-ENGINE]

  seed = "The mitosis engine learns online from scratch (@D p8, NO train/infer split — it keeps dividing during inference). Feeding a TIME-ORDERED stream (real text bytes / synthetic audio frames) in, what should GATE the cell-division growth tick (engine_mitosis_tick, CORE/engine_cli.hexa)? Three candidate tick-gates: METRONOME (M2-like, split every N steps on a fixed exogenous clock), POSITIONAL (M1-like, split keyed to absolute stream index), DERIVATIVE (M3-like, split on a rising-edge of |d(input)/dt| — the data's own CHANGE events). Plus a NO-GATE control (blind fixed-count split, input-ignoring). ELEVATES the toy-EEG finding of .discoveries/clm-time-encoding.tape (M3 DERIVATIVE was the ONLY arm to beat the phase-shuffled control there) + kosmos-time-axis (F-ORDER beats F-SHUFFLE) + tensionlink-dim-time (dF/dt beats shuffle) — to the GENERAL tick-gating question on a time-ordered text/audio stream, but on the falsifier-mandated SUBSTRATE-NATIVE ONLINE NEXT-STEP PREDICTION ERROR metric (NOT the decode/recon metric the toy-EEG win used)."

  method = "Reuse the H_1159/H_1159b prototype-split MITOSIS substrate (cells = prototype vectors, online-mean update, tension-driven split of the highest-tension cell, NO backprop/gradients per p8) as the ENGINE; swap ONLY the split-trigger gate among {METRONOME, POSITIONAL, DERIVATIVE, NOGATE}. All gates are split-BUDGET-matched (≈ expected derivative-fire count) and split the SAME (highest-tension) cell, isolating WHEN the tick fires as the only variable. Capacity kept SCARCE (MAX_CELLS=6) so split-PLACEMENT is testable. STREAMS: (1) TEXT [decisive] = real bytes in time-order from CORE/testdata/clm_mid_5lang_c4.txt (seed = deterministic start offset, NO shuffle/epochs), feature = 8-d local byte-statistics over a sliding 48-byte window, derivative = |d(feature)/dt| = byte-change/novelty; (2) AUDIO [confirmation] = synthetic RECURRING-REGIME drift stream (6 regimes each w/ own center+constant drift, revisited; a single global next-delta cannot serve all). METRIC = substrate-native ONLINE NEXT-STEP prediction error ||pred_next − true_next|| where pred_next = current + owner-cell running next-delta (p7, NOT perplexity/CE); ORDER-SENSITIVITY via a time-SHUFFLE control on the scored region. 10 seeds (900..909), deterministic, $0 CPU numpy. PRE-SCORING DEFECT-FIX (a_completeness_over_cheap, NOT a goalpost move): a diagnostic showed next-step error is NOISE-FLOORED and INVISIBLE to cell-count on a smooth feature stream (err ~flat 2→32 cells) → would make the gate untestable; fixed by SCARCE capacity + the recurring-regime audio stream where capacity provably matters. Frozen falsifier bars UNCHANGED."

  falsifier = "Pre-registered in the harness docstring BEFORE measuring; deterministic ≥8 seeds; paired Cohen's d on per-seed deltas (positive d => derivative is lower-error). F1 DERIVATIVE-WINS: on the ordered stream derivative beats BOTH metronome AND positional, d≥0.8 each. F2 ORDER-SENSITIVE: derivative-vs-metronome advantage VANISHES on the time-SHUFFLED control, d_shuf<0.3. F3 TICK-NECESSITY (the user's literal question): derivative beats the input-blind NO-GATE baseline, d≥0.8 → a tick IS needed AND should be event/derivative-driven; if metronome ties derivative AND both tie no-gate → 'a blind clock suffices' (honest negative). SUPPORTED (🟢 EVENT-DERIVATIVE-TICK) iff F1 ∧ F2 ∧ F3-derivative-beats-nogate; else CLOSED-NEGATIVE with the specific ruling."

  result = "🔴 CLOSED-NEGATIVE — NO event/derivative tick advantage under next-step error at toy scale; a blind clock roughly suffices. TEXT [decisive]: all 4 gates TIE at err≈0.742 (METRO 0.7437, POS 0.7424, DERIV 0.7416, NOGATE 0.7437). F1 FAIL derivative-vs-metronome d=0.15, vs-positional d=0.06 (≪0.8). F2 FAIL the tiny advantage SURVIVES/GROWS on shuffle (d_shuf=0.56≥0.3) — it's noise, not real temporal structure. F3 FAIL derivative-vs-nogate d=0.15 (<0.8); NOGATE ≡ METRONOME EXACTLY (both blind clocks, same budget → d=0.00) = the literal 'blind clock suffices' branch. AUDIO [confirmation] AGREES: derivative is actually WORSE (vs-metro d=−0.49, vs-pos d=−0.18, vs-nogate d=−0.49), shuffle d=1.34. supported=False, audio_agrees=False."

  finding = "The WHEN of the from-scratch mitosis growth-tick BARELY CHANGES online next-step prediction error at toy scale — metronome, positional, derivative and even a fully input-blind no-gate all land within noise of each other. So under the next-step-error metric the answer to 틱이 있어야 되나? is: NO special tick-gating is needed; a blind clock roughly suffices, and event/derivative-driven gating gives NO advantage (it even hurts on the recurring-regime audio stream). KEY DISTINCTION (reconciles with the prior toy-EEG win): clm-time-encoding's M3 DERIVATIVE win was on a DECODE/RECON metric (cells born under distinct regimes → stage-decode 1.0), NOT next-step error. Next-step prediction is NOISE-FLOORED and capacity-INVISIBLE (diagnostic: err flat 2→32 cells), so it CANNOT see the placement signal that decode/recon could. The derivative tick may still matter for regime-decode/recon while being near-irrelevant for next-step prediction — these are DIFFERENT axes (parallels H_1146 confidence-as-coherence ⊥ corpus-presence; metric-axis matters)."

  honest = "p7/g5, NO perplexity/CE (substrate-native next-step-error + shuffle order-sensitivity). NOT a goalpost move: the frozen F1/F2/F3 d≥0.8 / d_shuf<0.3 bars are verbatim from pre-registration; the only pre-scoring change was a DEFECT-FIX (scarce capacity + recurring-regime audio) to make the gate TESTABLE after a diagnostic proved next-step error is capacity-blind on a smooth stream — without that fix every arm would trivially tie and the test would be vacuous. Nulls NOT rounded into a HOLD: all 3 falsifiers fail on BOTH streams; the small positive text d's are reported as failures and shown to be shuffle-surviving noise. The decisive arm is TEXT (real bytes); AUDIO is a non-blocking confirmation and AGREES. Scope: TOY ONLY (a_toy_scale_recheck, a_scale_honest_scope) — live CORE engine_mitosis_tick (CORE/engine_cli.hexa) was NOT driven (next rung), real-audio (vs synthetic) + production scale UNVERIFIED. Lane-M gradient-free growth lane, recorded SEPARATELY from Lane A AKIDA / Lane G forge / Lane P torch (a_lane_akida_gpu_split). The honest residual: a next-step-error metric is the wrong instrument to detect a tick-placement effect; a decode/recon re-test of the tick-gate (per clm-time-encoding) would be the decisive follow-up."

  target = "🔴 CLOSED-NEGATIVE (a_paper_negative_ok). Specific ruling: under online NEXT-STEP prediction error, a blind clock suffices to gate the mitosis growth-tick — no metronome-vs-derivative-vs-no-gate distinction survives at toy scale, RULING OUT 'event/derivative tick is necessary for next-step prediction'. Distinct from (does NOT contradict) the toy-EEG decode/recon d/dt win — metric-axis dependent."

  note = "harness UNIVERSE/h1160_derivative_gated_tick.py ; verdict .verdicts/1160_derivative_gated_tick/H_1160.txt ; reuses UNIVERSE/h1159*.py substrate. xref clm-time-encoding · kosmos-time-axis · tensionlink-dim-time · h1159 · h1159b · p8 · a_paper_negative_ok · a_toy_scale_recheck · a_scale_honest_scope · a_lane_akida_gpu_split · p7."
